# Design system components

Unless the user specifies otherwise, build UI with the shared primitives catalogued on `/components`.

## Use these sources

| Control | Shared source |
|---------|----------------|
| Button | MUI `Button` — primary (contained), neutral (outlined inherit), tertiary/ghost (`text` + `primary`) |
| Icon button | `AppIconButton` — variants: `primary`, `secondary`, `emphasis`; radius 8/10/12 by size |
| Tab menu | `pillTabsSx` / `underlineTabsSx` (`src/components/ui/tabMenuStyles.ts`) |
| Nav menu item | `AppNavMenuItem` (`src/components/ui/AppNavMenuItem.tsx`) |
| Text field | `AppTextField` — S/M/L heights, 8px radius, label above, `outlined` \| `filled` |
| Dropdown | `AppSelectField` — same field rules as text |
| Search field | `AppSearchField` — same field rules + search icon |
| Switch | `AppSwitch` — inset knob; sizes `small` (28px) and `medium` (36px) |

Import from `src/components/ui` when available.

## Components page = global QA surface

`ComponentsPage.tsx` is a **viewer only** — it imports shared primitives, never one-off demo styling.

Canvas edits on the Components page must update the shared module or theme, not local page `sx`.

## Defaults

- Button / field heights: 28px (S), 36px (M), 44px (L)
- Neutral buttons: light outline (`NEUTRAL_BUTTON_BORDER_*`) + tactile depth
- Filled fields: `rgba(0,0,0,0.05)` background, no border
- Exceptions: visit note toolbar + Notarize Sign button (`visit-note-button-exempt`)
- Inline link actions: `BUTTON_LINK_CLASS` on text buttons
